cuda_kernel modules go to the disk kernel cache like MLX's own JIT kernels (MLX passes
use_disk_cache = false for them), so NVRTC compiles each once per machine instead of once per
process. The module name is `{kernel name}_{source_hash}`: since ml-explore/mlx#4568 the hash is
the one the CustomKernel carries (computed once per generated source, std::hash of the full
source), so this patch only turns the write on and hashes nothing itself. mlx-serve keys the
cache directory by its MLX build stamp, so a cached module never outlives its source or its
headers.

Retires when upstream caches custom kernels on disk. Not reported upstream yet.

--- a/mlx/backend/cuda/custom_kernel.cpp
+++ b/mlx/backend/cuda/custom_kernel.cpp
@@ -302,7 +302,8 @@
         return std::make_tuple(
             is_precompiled_, source_, std::vector{kernel_name});
       },
-      false);
+      // Cached on disk too: the module name hashes the generated source.
+      true);
 
   // Make the arguments
   cu::KernelArgs args;
